  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'One player leads a double as the spinner. Players must complete all four arms of the spinner before adding tiles to them. On your turn you may play a matching tile or draw from the boneyard until you can play or it is empty; if you can neither play nor draw, pass. Play until someone empties their hand (dominoes) or the game blocks.',
    Player: 'One player leads a double as the spinner. Players must complete all four arms of the spinner before adding tiles to them. On your turn you may play a matching tile or draw from the boneyard until you can play or it is empty; if you can neither play nor draw, pass. Play until someone empties their hand (dominoes) or the game blocks.',
    objective: 'Score points by making the ends of the cross-shaped layout match; first player to reach 100 points wins the game.',
    gameplay: 'One player leads a double as the spinner. Players must complete all four arms of the spinner before adding tiles to them. On your turn you may play a matching tile or draw from the boneyard until you can play or it is empty; if you can neither play nor draw, pass. Play until someone empties their hand (dominoes) or the game blocks.',
    keyRules: [
      'First double led is the spinner; all arms must be started before adding to any arm.',
      'Draw from boneyard when unable to play; pass when unable to play and unable to draw.',
      'Score after each play: pair of ends 2, triplet 3, quadruplet 4, quintuplet 5.',
      'At round end deduct 1 point per tile left in hand; player who dominoes deducts nothing.',
      'Game is 100 points.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two to four players. Two players receive six tiles each; three players six each; four players five each. Remaining tiles form the boneyard.',
