      'Turn-flow example: One player leads a double as the spinner. Players must complete all four arms of the spinner before adding tiles to them. On your turn you may play a matching tile or draw from the boneyard until you can play or it is empty; if you can neither play nor draw, pass. Play until someone empties their hand (dominoes) or the game blocks.',
